[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186115357 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115358 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115359 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" "question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115360 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" "question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/id #uuid "b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251067" :question/problem "![](images/45/45ab2798a4635050c736dadeeef49baa8ac46119c1ec797baa1c85116dd5c0d7.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =\\frac{7}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =7 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =13.165…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot (13.165…) \\\\  & =46.077… \\\\  & ≈46,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/id #uuid "ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/id #uuid "6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/math-academy-id "q-76772" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5ff3d7cda0ee3fbc807a4bacbd3a739d72d83d0020271936ba77e6afbc89b83f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{5}{8},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{5}{8}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & =\\frac{3x-2}{4x} \\\\ 5(4x) & =8(3x-2) \\\\ 20x & =24x-16 \\\\ -4x & =-16 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x-2=3(4)-2=10, \\\\ AC & =4x=4(4)=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" "answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" "answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" "answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/id #uuid "10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/id #uuid "c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "140" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/id #uuid "03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/id #uuid "f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/id #uuid "d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/id #uuid "103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-54311" :question/problem "![](images/93/93489f5dd12c8dbbde799b4047965a89e4204f151c0b4dfc36286392775a05e2.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ where $\\theta =m∠C.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠C.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AB}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{AB}{8} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\ AB & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/id #uuid "212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" "answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" "answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" "answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/id #uuid "144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/id #uuid "8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/id #uuid "bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/id #uuid "78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/id #uuid "97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/id #uuid "e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/math-academy-id "q-54310" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d996bfd2f4fa9822cae6284a3168f20911dbfd735a9b9c3c261fd30262b08e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{AC}{10} \\\\ AC & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 10 \\\\ AC & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" "answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" "answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" "answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/id #uuid "06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/id #uuid "83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/id #uuid "58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/id #uuid "c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/id #uuid "ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/id #uuid "37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124469" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb14c05b065e8f3745dd6f1f3ad793abef565dac91047a89663c588519eabaaf.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3) & =3\\cdot 2x \\\\ 3x+3\\sqrt{3} & =6x \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3=\\sqrt{3}\\,(\\sqrt{3})+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" "answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" "answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" "answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/id #uuid "53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/id #uuid "d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/id #uuid "a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/id #uuid "a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/id #uuid "77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/id #uuid "a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-251195" :question/problem "![](images/24/243d382164750cdeb771f8630c3df642abcb034b3ddeb3c919f0b5f6b4fbff33.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={72}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+4}{2x-1} \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =3x+4 \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =3x+4 \\\\ x(2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-3) & =4+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{4+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})}{2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-3} \\\\ x & =2.243\\,0…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x-1=2(2.243\\,0…)-1=3.486\\,1…, \\\\ AC & =3x+4=3(2.243\\,0…)+4=10.729\\,1….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(10.729\\,1…)(3.486\\,1…) \\\\  & =18.701\\,3… \\\\  & ≈18.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/id #uuid "465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/id #uuid "069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116453 :tutorial/content "Consider the right triangle $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f7de9810f4acf33b504eb010d641e99811de82eed919e4340b5e68d414269ca.png)\n\nThe area of this right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = \\dfrac 1 2 ab.\n$$\n\nBut how can we calculate the area if we only know one side and one angle, as in the triangle below? \n\n![](images/c1/c1e5331333639f4d8e4f7b4cb3fee30ed1a7a889968844ae2b10961c5ae8e3ef.png)\n\nWe can follow the two steps below.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the missing side using the trigonometric ratios.\n\nHere, we need the adjacent side, and we know the opposite side. So, we should use tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ BC\\sqrt{3} & =9 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ BC & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Use the formula to calculate the area.\n\nNow that we know both sides of the triangle, we can just apply the formula as usual and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115434 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/id #uuid "b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d"] ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251067"] ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/problem "![](images/45/45ab2798a4635050c736dadeeef49baa8ac46119c1ec797baa1c85116dd5c0d7.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}."] ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =\\frac{7}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =7 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =13.165…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot (13.165…) \\\\  & =46.077… \\\\  & ≈46,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."] ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf"] ["answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/id #uuid "ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456"] ["answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/value "46"] ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/correct "answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456"] ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/choices "answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456"] ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf"] [17592186115357 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d"] ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/id #uuid "6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07"] ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/math-academy-id "q-76772"] ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5ff3d7cda0ee3fbc807a4bacbd3a739d72d83d0020271936ba77e6afbc89b83f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{5}{8},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above."] ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{5}{8}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & =\\frac{3x-2}{4x} \\\\ 5(4x) & =8(3x-2) \\\\ 20x & =24x-16 \\\\ -4x & =-16 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x-2=3(4)-2=10, \\\\ AC & =4x=4(4)=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12"] ["answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/id #uuid "10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956"] ["answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/value "100"] ["answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/id #uuid "c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396"] ["answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/value "140"] ["answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/id #uuid "03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd"] ["answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/value "70"] ["answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/id #uuid "f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c"] ["answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/value "80"] ["answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/id #uuid "d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d"] ["answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/value "90"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/correct "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/choices "answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/choices "answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/choices "answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/choices "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c"] ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/choices "answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d"] ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12"] [17592186115358 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07"] ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/id #uuid "103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59"] ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-54311"] ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/problem "![](images/93/93489f5dd12c8dbbde799b4047965a89e4204f151c0b4dfc36286392775a05e2.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above."] ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ where $\\theta =m∠C.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠C.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AB}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{AB}{8} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\ AB & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/id #uuid "212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622"] ["answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/id #uuid "144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a"] ["answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/value "12"] ["answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/id #uuid "8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f"] ["answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/value "16"] ["answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/id #uuid "bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c"] ["answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/value "18"] ["answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/id #uuid "78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f"] ["answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/value "24"] ["answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/id #uuid "97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b"] ["answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/value "32"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/correct "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/choices "answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/choices "answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/choices "answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/choices "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f"] ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/choices "answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b"] ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622"] [17592186115359 :knowledge-point/questions "question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59"] ["question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/id #uuid "e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db"] ["question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/math-academy-id "q-54310"] ["question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d996bfd2f4fa9822cae6284a3168f20911dbfd735a9b9c3c261fd30262b08e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above."] ["question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{AC}{10} \\\\ AC & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 10 \\\\ AC & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9"] ["answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/id #uuid "06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00"] ["answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/value "20"] ["answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/id #uuid "83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4"] ["answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/value "35"] ["answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/id #uuid "58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b"] ["answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/value "40"] ["answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/id #uuid "c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5"] ["answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/value "45"] ["answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/id #uuid "ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303"] ["answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/value "50"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/correct "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5"] ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303"] ["question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9"] [17592186115359 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db"] ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/id #uuid "37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f"] ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124469"] ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb14c05b065e8f3745dd6f1f3ad793abef565dac91047a89663c588519eabaaf.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above."] ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3) & =3\\cdot 2x \\\\ 3x+3\\sqrt{3} & =6x \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3=\\sqrt{3}\\,(\\sqrt{3})+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc"] ["answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/id #uuid "53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe"] ["answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/id #uuid "d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38"] ["answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}"] ["answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/id #uuid "a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7"] ["answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/id #uuid "a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e"] ["answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}"] ["answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/id #uuid "77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e"] ["answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/correct "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/choices "answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/choices "answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/choices "answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/choices "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e"] ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/choices "answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e"] ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc"] [17592186115360 :knowledge-point/questions "question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f"] ["question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/id #uuid "a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea"] ["question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-251195"] ["question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/problem "![](images/24/243d382164750cdeb771f8630c3df642abcb034b3ddeb3c919f0b5f6b4fbff33.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}."] ["question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={72}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+4}{2x-1} \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =3x+4 \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =3x+4 \\\\ x(2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-3) & =4+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{4+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})}{2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-3} \\\\ x & =2.243\\,0…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x-1=2(2.243\\,0…)-1=3.486\\,1…, \\\\ AC & =3x+4=3(2.243\\,0…)+4=10.729\\,1….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(10.729\\,1…)(3.486\\,1…) \\\\  & =18.701\\,3… \\\\  & ≈18.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."] ["question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/id #uuid "465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e"] ["answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/id #uuid "069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa"] ["answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/value "18.7"] ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/correct "answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa"] ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/choices "answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa"] ["question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e"] [17592186115360 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea"] [17592186116453 :tutorial/content "Consider the right triangle $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f7de9810f4acf33b504eb010d641e99811de82eed919e4340b5e68d414269ca.png)\n\nThe area of this right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = \\dfrac 1 2 ab.\n$$\n\nBut how can we calculate the area if we only know one side and one angle, as in the triangle below? \n\n![](images/c1/c1e5331333639f4d8e4f7b4cb3fee30ed1a7a889968844ae2b10961c5ae8e3ef.png)\n\nWe can follow the two steps below.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the missing side using the trigonometric ratios.\n\nHere, we need the adjacent side, and we know the opposite side. So, we should use tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ BC\\sqrt{3} & =9 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ BC & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Use the formula to calculate the area.\n\nNow that we know both sides of the triangle, we can just apply the formula as usual and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115434 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0]] "retractions" [[17592186116453 :tutorial/content "Consider the right triangle $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f7de9810f4acf33b504eb010d641e99811de82eed919e4340b5e68d414269ca.png)\n\nThe area of this right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = \\dfrac 1 2 ab.\n$$\n\nBut how can we calculate the area if we only know one side and one angle, as in the triangle below? \n\n![](images/c1/c1e5331333639f4d8e4f7b4cb3fee30ed1a7a889968844ae2b10961c5ae8e3ef.png)\n\nWe can follow the two steps below.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the missing side using the trigonometric ratios.\n\nHere, we need the adjacent side, and we know the opposite side. So, we should use tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}(B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}{30}^{∘} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ BC\\sqrt{3} & =9 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ BC & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Use the formula to calculate the area.\n\nNow that we know both sides of the triangle, we can just apply the formula as usual and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]}]